description: ARTHUR WELLESLEY / DUKE OF WELLINGTON/ BORN 1769. DIED 1852. // WISDOM   DUTY  HONOUR

Not visible in images
The following has been adopted for the inscription on the Wellington monument, in the Guildhall, London &quot;This monument erected in grateful memory of Arthur Wellesley, who served his country at home and abroad, in peace and war, sixty-three years. Wisdom, duty, honour.&quot;
